[{"name":"Bill Shankly","role":"Manager","years":"1959–1974","caps":null,"goals":null,"image":"/assets/lfc/legends/bill-shankly.jpg","bio":"The man who built modern Liverpool. Shankly transformed a struggling Second Division club into a formidable First Division force, winning three league titles, two FA Cups and the UEFA Cup. His philosophy — 'football is not just a matter of life and death, it is much more important than that' — lives on at Anfield."},{"name":"Bob Paisley","role":"Manager","years":"1974–1983","caps":null,"goals":null,"image":"/assets/lfc/legends/bob-paisley.jpg","bio":"The most decorated manager in Liverpool's history. Paisley won six league titles, three European Cups, three League Cups and one UEFA Cup in nine seasons — a record that may never be surpassed. Quiet, modest and tactically brilliant."},{"name":"Kenny Dalglish","role":"Forward / Manager","years":"1977–1990","caps":515,"goals":172,"image":"/assets/lfc/legends/kenny-dalglish.jpg","bio":"Widely regarded as Liverpool's greatest ever player. Dalglish scored the winning goal in the 1978 European Cup final and later led the club as player-manager to a legendary league and FA Cup double in 1986. A true legend of Anfield."},{"name":"Steven Gerrard","role":"Midfielder","years":"1998–2015","caps":710,"goals":186,"image":"/assets/lfc/legends/steven-gerrard.jpg","bio":"The heartbeat of Liverpool for 17 years. Gerrard inspired the Miracle of Istanbul with a second-half header and played with passion and leadership in every game he wore the red shirt. One of the finest midfielders of his generation."},{"name":"Ian Rush","role":"Striker","years":"1980–1996","caps":660,"goals":346,"image":"/assets/lfc/legends/ian-rush.jpg","bio":"Liverpool's all-time leading goal scorer. Rush was a relentless predator in the penalty area, winning five league titles and three FA Cups. His partnership with Kenny Dalglish was one of the most lethal in English football history."},{"name":"Robbie Fowler","role":"Striker","years":"1993–2001 / 2006–2007","caps":369,"goals":183,"image":"/assets/lfc/legends/robbie-fowler.jpg","bio":"Known as 'God' on the Kop, Fowler's natural finishing ability made him one of the deadliest strikers of his era. He scored 25 league goals in his first full season and went on to become a Liverpool icon."},{"name":"Jamie Carragher","role":"Defender","years":"1996–2013","caps":737,"goals":4,"image":"/assets/lfc/legends/jamie-carragher.jpg","bio":"Carra was a warrior at the heart of Liverpool's defence for 17 years. His performances in Istanbul in 2005 were heroic. A born leader and one of the best defenders of his generation who dedicated his career entirely to Liverpool."},{"name":"Graeme Souness","role":"Midfielder","years":"1978–1984","caps":359,"goals":56,"image":"/assets/lfc/legends/graeme-souness.jpg","bio":"One of the most complete midfielders in English football history. Souness was the engine of the all-conquering Liverpool teams of the late 1970s and early 1980s, winning five league titles and three European Cups."},{"name":"Mohamed Salah","role":"Forward","years":"2017–present","caps":432,"goals":254,"image":"/assets/lfc/legends/mohamed-salah.jpg","bio":"The Egyptian King. Salah broke the Premier League single-season record with 32 goals in 2017/18 and has been Liverpool's most consistent match-winner ever since. A Champions League winner in 2019, Premier League champion in 2020 and 2025. Liverpool's third all-time top scorer."},{"name":"Virgil van Dijk","role":"Defender","years":"2018–present","caps":357,"goals":32,"image":"/assets/lfc/legends/virgil-van-dijk.jpg","bio":"The best centre-back in the world at his peak. Van Dijk's arrival transformed Liverpool's defensive record and was central to winning the Champions League and Premier League. A commanding presence and superb leader."},{"name":"Jürgen Klopp","role":"Manager","years":"2015–2024","caps":null,"goals":null,"image":"/assets/lfc/legends/jurgen-klopp.jpg","bio":"The 'Normal One'. Klopp arrived in 2015 and built a team capable of conquering Europe and England. He delivered Liverpool's first Champions League in 14 years, the FIFA Club World Cup and ended the 30-year wait for a league title. Left with eight trophies and eternal love from the Kop."},{"name":"Luis Suárez","role":"Striker","years":"2011–2014","caps":133,"goals":82,"image":"/assets/lfc/legends/luis-suarez.jpg","bio":"One of the most electrifying players ever to wear the red shirt. Suárez terrorised Premier League defences with his relentless movement, invention and ruthless finishing. His 2013/14 season — 31 league goals in 33 games — almost single-handedly delivered the title before a heartbreaking final-day collapse. Left for Barcelona having become a Liverpool legend in just three seasons."},{"name":"Alisson Becker","role":"Goalkeeper","years":"2018–present","caps":300,"goals":1,"image":"/assets/lfc/legends/alisson-becker.jpg","bio":"The world's best goalkeeper and the final piece of Klopp's jigsaw. Alisson's £65m arrival from Roma transformed Liverpool's defensive record. He famously scored a headed goal against West Brom in 2021 to help clinch a Champions League spot. A Champions League winner in 2019 and Premier League champion in 2020 and 2025, he is widely regarded as the finest goalkeeper in the club's history."},{"name":"Kevin Keegan","role":"Forward","years":"1971–1977","caps":323,"goals":100,"image":"/assets/lfc/legends/kevin-keegan.jpg","bio":"Two-time Ballon d'Or winner and one of the most exciting forwards in Liverpool's history. Keegan arrived from Scunthorpe United for £33,000 in 1971 and formed a devastating partnership with John Toshack, helping Liverpool win three league titles, the FA Cup, two UEFA Cups and the European Cup. Left for Hamburg in 1977 and won back-to-back European Footballer of the Year awards."},{"name":"Jordan Henderson","role":"Midfielder","years":"2011–2023","caps":492,"goals":33,"image":"/assets/lfc/legends/jordan-henderson.jpg","bio":"Liverpool's captain during their most glorious modern era. Henderson lifted the Champions League, Premier League, FA Cup, League Cup and FIFA Club World Cup as skipper, becoming the first Liverpool captain to raise the league title in 30 years. His infectious leadership and relentless dedication over 12 years made him one of the most important players in the club's history."},{"name":"John Barnes","role":"Winger","years":"1987–1997","caps":407,"goals":108,"image":"/assets/lfc/legends/john-barnes.jpg","bio":"One of the most talented players ever to grace Anfield. Barnes arrived from Watford in 1987 and lit up English football with his extraordinary pace, skill and creativity. He won two league titles and two FA Cups, and was named FWA Footballer of the Year twice. His mesmerising dribbling and devastating finishing made him one of the greatest wingers in English football history."}]